#!/usr/bin/env sh
#MISE description="Show this workflow cheat sheet (runs on bare 'mise run')"
#MISE quiet=true
set -eu
cat <<'EOF'
cur8s.ubuntu labs — full details: docs/operations/manual.md

GRAMMAR: every task is   mise run <provider>:<object>:<action>

  providers
    qemu    local QEMU VM (free, arm64)
    do      DigitalOcean droplet (amd64)

  objects
    vm      the machine itself       create, boot, wait, status, destroy, ...
    play    a collection playbook    converge, update, validate-reboot, ...
    ssh     a shell, as this user    ansible, sysadmin, root
    test    an example, or all       docker, k3s, zot, ..., all

  workflows (no object — the provider itself is the object)
    prep    one-time groundwork
    up      provision + converge

  Same grammar on every provider: swap qemu: for do: and it just works.

A SESSION, START TO FINISH (local provider shown)

  mise run qemu:prep             once: 1Password keys + cloud image cache (~600MB)
  mise run qemu:up               stand up the lab, unattended
                                 (= vm:create -> vm:boot -> vm:wait -> play:converge)
  mise run qemu:vm:status        where am I? stages done, and the next command
  mise run qemu:ssh:ansible      inspect by hand (boot problems: qemu:vm:console)
  mise run qemu:play:converge    daily re-assert; changed=0 means conformant
  mise run qemu:test:docker      test one example: runs it twice,
                                 second pass must report changed=0
  mise run qemu:test:all         every example, same contract
  mise run qemu:play:validate-reboot   acceptance gate: reboot, re-verify access
  mise run qemu:vm:destroy       tear down; the cached image survives

  Droplet extras: do:ssh:root is the provider bootstrap door — until
  do:play:retire-bootstrap locks it (run the acceptance gate first).

  clean  destroy both labs + wipe .generated        mise tasks  the full list
EOF
